  cruzamento: `THE CROSS-READING OF JUL 31 ended with the front-runner where he had never been. Lula ROSE 1.00pp and went to 64.50% (vol USD 7.77M), passing for the first time since Apr 14 the 63.50% the AFOS series had been matching without exceeding on Jul 26, 28, 30 and 31. Flávio ROSE 0.40pp, to 24.35% (vol USD 7.76M), and even so the gap WIDENED from +39.55pp to +40.15pp, the widest in the series that holds both names, which begins on May 3 and whose previous maximum was +39.80pp on Jul 26. It is the first reading above 40pp. The distinction matters and the panel makes it: the gap widened with the opponent ALSO rising, which describes demand for the front-runner and not deterioration on the other side. `
    + `THE POLL. Vox Brasil of Jul 31 (n=2,100, field Jul 26 to 28, margin of 2.15pp, 95% confidence, BR-01084/2026) gives Lula 40.5% x Flávio 31.2% in the [first round](/en/glossary#primeiro-turno), with Caiado 5.5%, Zema 3.2% and Renan Santos 3.0%, and Lula 47.5% x Flávio 41.1% in the [runoff](/en/glossary#segundo-turno). The 6.4pp advantage in the runoff falls OUTSIDE the two margins added together, so this reading does NOT describe a statistical tie, unlike PoderData of Jul 30. And the record that organizes the week is this: THREE houses measured the first-round gap at 9.1pp, 6pp and 9.3pp. Two agree around 9pp and the outlier is PoderData. On Jul 30 the panel wrote, correctly, that comparing different houses and calling the difference movement is swapping rulers; today's Vox reinforces that discipline by another route, showing that PoderData was the one outside the set. `
